    <string name="faq_1_question">How do I make Foss Explorer my default browser?</string>
    <string name="faq_1_answer">Open the settings of your device, go to Apps, then Default apps, then Browser app, and choose Foss Explorer.</string>
    <string name="faq_2_question">Where are my downloads?</string>
    <string name="faq_2_answer">The three-dot menu has a Downloads entry that lists what this browser downloaded. The files are in the Downloads folder of your device.</string>
    <string name="faq_3_question">What is a private tab?</string>
    <string name="faq_3_answer">A private tab does not write to the history and is not restored when the browser starts again. Whether it also keeps its cookies apart from normal tabs depends on the WebView of your device; a message says which applies when you open one.</string>
    <string name="faq_4_question">How do I block ads?</string>
    <string name="faq_4_answer">Open Site settings, then Ads. While the switch there is off, ads and trackers are blocked with the filter list you choose on the same screen. With \"Add site exception\" you can allow them for a single site.</string>
    <string name="faq_5_question">Why do websites think I use Google Chrome?</string>
    <string name="faq_5_answer">Many websites work badly, or not at all, with browsers they do not know. Foss Explorer therefore introduces itself as Chrome on Android, with the Android version of your device. The Desktop site switch in the three-dot menu makes it introduce itself as Chrome on a computer instead.</string>
    <string name="faq_6_question">I hid the bars. How do I get them back?</string>
    <string name="faq_6_answer">Tap the small round button in the top corner of the page.</string>
    <string name="faq_7_question">How do I move my bookmarks to another device?</string>
    <string name="faq_7_answer">Use Backup in the settings to save your data to a file, copy the file to the other device, and restore it there with Backup.</string>
    <string name="about_fork_title">Code from FOSS Browser</string>
    <string name="about_fork_summary">I started Foss Explorer as a fork of FOSS Browser by Gaukler Faun. Since then I have rebuilt its screens after Chromium and Firefox, I keep history and bookmarks in a database laid out like Firefox\'s, and I keep the list of open tabs the way Chromium does. I still use FOSS Browser\'s code for the bookmark filter, the gestures and the backup, and for the parts that load and filter pages: the web view inside a tab, the ad and cookie-banner blockers and the site profiles. That code stays under the AGPL, and I list it under Open source components.</string>
